CON-09: keep pollutant in ponded surface water when the water evaporates

The ponded-quality block of the runoff step rebuilt the ponded mass from
the end-of-step depth, as 5.3.0 does, so pollutant in evaporated water
was dropped. Keep the mass that infiltration and runoff did not remove.
6.0.0 also zeroed the ponded mass of a surface that dried without booking
it, and left the mass still ponded at the end out of Remaining Buildup.
Book the dried-out mass to a new running total, qual_final_ponded_dry
(MassBalance, next to qual_routing_final_dry), and add it and the ponded
mass to Remaining Buildup in computeFinalQualityMassBalance(), as legacy's
FINAL_LOAD and massbal_getBuildup() do.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-09_swmm600.patch

